== sanity: sanity_check/test_generation.py ==
Generation sanity check
TinyStepModel returns very high logits for scripted next-token IDs.
This checks decoding mechanics, not text quality.

Note: CHECK_LOG=1 disables ANSI colors in saved logs.

Case 1: PASS top-p keeps at least the highest-probability token
  logits:         [[0.10000000149011612, 8.0, 0.20000000298023224, 2.0]]
  top_p:          0.01
  expected shape: (1, 1)
  actual shape:   (1, 1)
  expected token: [[1]]
  actual token:   [[1]]

Case 2: PASS plain multinomial sampling supports batched logits
  logits:         [[0.10000000149011612, 3.0, 0.20000000298023224, 2.0], [4.0, 0.10000000149011612, 0.20000000298023224, 0.30000001192092896]]
  logits shape:   (2, 4)
  expected shape: (2, 1)
  actual shape:   (2, 1)
  sampled tokens: [[1], [0]]

Case 3: PASS decode appends tokens until eos
  prompt:         [[0, 4, 4]]
  scripted next:  [1, 2]
  fake logits:    selected token gets 20.0, all others get -20.0
  expected:       [[0, 4, 4, 1, 2]]
  actual:         [[0, 4, 4, 1, 2]]

Case 4: PASS decode respects max_new_tokens when eos is absent
  prompt:         [[0, 4]]
  scripted next:  [1, 3, 4]
  fake logits:    selected token gets 20.0, all others get -20.0
  expected:       [[0, 4, 1, 3, 4]]
  actual:         [[0, 4, 1, 3, 4]]

Case 5: PASS max_new_tokens=0 returns the prompt without model calls
  prompt:         [[0, 4]]
  fake logits:    not produced because model should not be called
  expected:       [[0, 4]]
  actual:         [[0, 4]]
  model calls:    0

Case 6: PASS context_length crops model input while keeping full output history
  fake logits:            selected token gets 20.0, all others get -20.0
  prompt length:          5
  context_length:         3
  expected max input len: 3
  actual input lengths:   [3, 3]
